<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/16th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Orsha</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1514</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muscovite-lithuanian-wars">Muscovite–Lithuanian Wars</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Orsha was fought on 8 September 1514 on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dnieper">Dnieper</a> near Orsha in modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belarus">Belarus</a>. A Polish-Lithuanian army under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hetman">Hetman</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/konstanty-ostrogski">Konstanty Ostrogski</a> defeated a larger Muscovite army, shortly after Vasily III had captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/smolensk">Smolensk</a>. The victory was widely celebrated in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> but did not recover Smolensk, which remained in Muscovite hands.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-orsha.jpg" alt="Battle of Orsha" width="320" height="201" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Attributed to Hans Krell · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Autor_nieznany_(malarz_z_kr%C4%99gu_Lukasa_Cranacha_Starszego),_Bitwa_pod_Orsz%C4%85.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
